From 12478b29ebf389a7a913c505f9c5dbea17c19911 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Brad Barnett <127794626+bdbarnett@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 22:53:01 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] tools/makemanifest.py: list C modules with forward slashes.

--list-c-modules prints each c_module() path as manifestfile resolved it,
with os.path.abspath, so on Windows it carries backslashes. py/manifest.mk
reads that list into USER_C_MODULES, and a module's micropython.mk that
runs a script from $(USERMOD_DIR) through the shell gets the path with its
backslashes dropped (C:\Users\... becomes C:Users...). Python and make both
take forward slashes on Windows, and the list is unchanged elsewhere.

Seen on a native Windows (MSYS2 MinGW) build of ports/windows with
audiodsp, whose micropython.mk runs $(USERMOD_DIR)/scripts/fetch_deps.sh.
Unchanged on upstream v1.29.0.
---
 tools/makemanifest.py | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/tools/makemanifest.py b/tools/makemanifest.py
index a149755..5f7903d 100644
--- a/tools/makemanifest.py
+++ b/tools/makemanifest.py
@@ -176,7 +176,9 @@ def main():
         if c_modules:
             # Output one path per line to handle paths with spaces
             for module in c_modules:
-                print(module)
+                # Forward slashes: make hands these to sh, which drops a
+                # Windows path's backslashes.
+                print(module.replace(os.sep, "/"))
         sys.exit(0)
 
     # Get paths to tools
-- 
2.54.0.windows.1

